## Root Cause
The test's Playwright `webServer` runs `docker compose up --build frontend`
(see `tests/playwright.config.ts`), and `docker-compose.yaml` builds the
`frontend` service from context `./services/frontend`. That directory does
not exist yet, so the Docker build fails, the server never comes up on
`http://127.0.0.1:3000`, and the test fails. The contract asserts that
navigating to `/` renders a single `<h1>` whose text is exactly
`Hello world`.

The fix is to create a minimal Next.js (App Router, TypeScript) service under
`services/frontend/` that builds in Docker and serves `<h1>Hello world</h1>`
at `/` on port 3000. All eight files below are NEW — use the Write tool for
each. Do not add `old_string` sections. Copy each file's content verbatim.

